{
  "pdf_page": 281,
  "book_page": 251,
  "verified_by": "claude-opus-5",
  "verified_on": "2026-09-06",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 0,
      "root": "Ksîp, Ksîph / Ksiptom, Ksiptis",
      "verdict": "plausible",
      "modern_form": "Two roots, not one: (a) PIE *ksei̯p-/*ksei̯b- 'to throw, hurl' (Walde-Pokorny I 501 qseip-, qseib-; Skt. kṣipáti) and (b) PIE *(k)su̯eip-/*su̯eib- 'to swing, shake, whip' (Pokorny 1041-42 su̯ei-b-/su̯ei-p-; LIV 377; Av. xšuuaēb-). Wiktionary's *ksweybʰ- 'to move swiftly, swing, whip, throw' is a modern attempt to unite them.",
      "note": "Nourai reproduces S. E. Mann's entry verbatim: IEC p. 573 has 'ksip- (ksiph-) \"strike; weapon, spike\"' with Skt. kṣipāmi, Av. xšip-, Myc. qisip-, Gk. ksiphos, Lat. sipillus, and the following entry 'ksiptom, is \"stab, wound\"'. The citation IEC:573 is exact (the leaf carries the running head 'kseul- — ksnt-' with '574' in the gutter, so ksip- is the left-hand column = p. 573). The reconstruction itself is Mann's private notation ('Ksîp' with a long î is not a normal PIE shape; there is no laryngeal/ablaut notation). Walde-Pokorny I 501 sets up qseip-, qseib- 'werfen, schwingend schleudern' for Skt. kṣipáti / OCS šibati and expressly calls the attempt to unite it with u̯eip-/-b- and sneip-/-b- through an initial qsu-/squ- 'wenig überzeugend'; Pokorny 1041-42 puts the Avestan material (xšuuaēwayat.aštra-, xšviwra-) under su̯ei-b- with no mention of kṣip-. Cheung (EDIV s.v. *xšuaip/b) is explicit: 'the semantic differences displayed by the Iranian forms favour the postulation of two different (Ir.) roots, *xšaip/b \"to throw, hurl\" and *xšuaip/b'. So the Iranian branch of this chart (šēb, nišēb, šiftan) belongs to the 'swing/shake' root, while the Sanskrit branch (kṣip-, kṣipta-) belongs to the 'throw' root; the Greek and Latin members do not belong to either. The root is therefore accepted as an approximation ('plausible'), not as a single well-formed etymon.",
      "note_fa": "نورایی این ریشه را عیناً از فرهنگ تطبیقی هندواروپایی استوارت مان (IEC، ص ۵۷۳) برداشته است؛ ارجاع او دقیق است. اما بازسازی «Ksîp» یک ریشهٔ استاندارد هندواروپایی نیست و پژوهش امروزی دو ریشهٔ جداگانه می‌شناسد: یکی *ksei̯p- «افکندن، پرتاب کردن» (والده-پوکورنی، ج۱ ص۵۰۱؛ سنسکریت kṣipáti) و دیگری *(k)su̯eip-/*su̯eib- «جنباندن، لرزاندن، تازیانه زدن» (پوکورنی ص۱۰۴۱–۱۰۴۲؛ اوستایی xšuuaēb-). چونگ در فرهنگ ریشه‌شناختی فعل ایرانی به‌صراحت می‌گوید تفاوت معنایی صورت‌های ایرانی ایجاب می‌کند دو ریشهٔ ایرانی جدا فرض شود: *xšaip/b «افکندن» و *xšuaip/b «جنبیدن». بنابراین شاخهٔ ایرانی این نمودار (شیب، نشیب، شیفتن) به ریشهٔ «جنبیدن» بازمی‌گردد و شاخهٔ سنسکریت به ریشهٔ «افکندن»؛ ادعای نورایی در کلیت با احتیاط پذیرفتنی است ولی یکی‌انگاشتن این دو ریشه پذیرفته نیست.",
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/ksweyb%CA%B0-",
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B7%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%8D"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {"ref": "IEC:573", "status": "supports", "note": "IEC.txt leaf 326 (printed pp. 573-574, running head 'kseul- (kseuel-) — ksnt-'): 'ksip- (ksiph-) \"strike; weapon, spike\". Cf. WP I, 380 & 449. (qusip- ?) Skt. ksipami \"throw, strike\"; Av. xšip-, id.; Myc. qisip-; Gk. cf. ksiphos, n. \"thrusting-sword\"; Alb. cf. shpoj …; Lat. cf. sipillus (dim. type: \"razor\"); OCS *šipŭ \"thorn\" …' and immediately after 'ksiptom, is \"stab, wound\" … Skt. ksiptám \"wound\"'. Nourai's root box (name, gloss, refs) is a faithful copy of this page."}
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {"src": "WLD", "where": "Bd. I p. 501 s.v. qseip-, qseib-", "stance": "partial", "note": "grep 'ksipati' in incoming/WLD/WLD_Bd1_pages.txt line 47280: 'qseip-, qseib- \"werfen, schwingend schleudern, in schwingender heftiger Bewegung sein\". Ai. ksipati \"wirft, schleudert\" … aksl. šiba-jǫ … russ. sibatĭ \"werfen\"'; and then 'Über den wenig überzeugenden Versuch, qseip-, -b- mit sneip-, -b- (ahd. sīfan, av. xšwiwra- usw.) und mit ueip, -b- … mittelst eines Anlautes qsu- oder squ- zu vermitteln …'. Walde-Pokorny thus keeps Skt. kṣip- apart from the Avestan xšu̯- material — the opposite of Nourai's single root."},
        {"src": "POK", "where": "pp. 1041-1042 s.v. su̯ei-, su̯ei-b-, su̯ei-p-", "stance": "partial", "note": "POK_03.txt lines 3940-3985: 'su̯ei(-) \"biegen, drehen, schwingen\" … *su̯eib-: av. xšvaewayat-aštra- \"die Peitsche schwingend\", xšviwra- \"flink\" … got. midja-sweipains \"Sintflut\"; aisl. sveipa \"werfen, umhüllen\" … su̯eip-: aisl. svífa \"schwingen, drehen\" … lett. svaipīt \"peitschen\"'. Pokorny houses the Avestan 'swing/whip' forms here and never mentions Skt. kṣip- in the entry."},
        {"src": "AHD", "where": "Watkins 1985 appendix", "stance": "silent", "note": "grep -i 'sweib|sweip|kseip|ksweibh' in AHD_watkins1985.txt: no hits. Watkins lists no root for this family (no English reflex)."},
        {"src": "CHEUNG", "where": "s.v. *xšuaip/b", "stance": "contradicts", "note": "CHEUNG.txt line 29673: 'Despite the obvious, formal similarities, the semantic differences displayed by the Iranian forms favour the postulation of two different (Ir.) roots, *xšaip/b \"to throw, hurl\" and *xšuaip/b respectively, cf. Panaino, Tiš. I: 96; EWAia I: 437. The root *xšaip/b can be connected to Skt. kṣep, whereas *xšuaip/b may be related to the IE \"swing, whip\" forms.' PIE given as '? *(k)sueip- \"to swing, shake, whip\" = LIV: 377 | Pok.: 1042'."},
        {"src": "SYN", "where": "20.27 'Sword'", "stance": "contradicts", "note": "SYN.txt line 34805: '1. Grk. ξίφος, prob. a loanword fr. the same source as Egypt. sft \"knife, sword\". Boisacq 679 with references.' Buck removes the Greek witness from any IE root."}
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Avestan / Old Persian",
          "words": "xšip, xšwaip, xšwaif; xšvaepâ",
